    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offensive engine today is anchored by **Gunnar Henderson** (81.88) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (77.95), both of whom benefit from optimal park factors and highly favorable matchups against N. Martinez and Rod\u00f3n, respectively. **Gunnar Henderson** is our premier play, boasting a massive 17% SP skill advantage and a dynamic platoon edge that elevates his daily efficiency well into our elite tier. Similarly, **Jackson Merrill** (75.27) stands out as a critical secondary target; while he faces the respectable Bailey Ober, his ability to exploit Ober\u2019s slow delivery\u2014driving a 92% SB success probability\u2014makes him a high-leverage asset in our scramble for stolen bases.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved the marginal 45.53 score assigned to **Miguel Vargas** and the surrounding bench. **Dominic Smith** (38.84) was the primary candidate to displace **Miguel Vargas**, but his L/L platoon disadvantage against Shane Drohan ultimately capped his utility. We have opted to stick with **Miguel Vargas** despite a mediocre projection because his projected spot in the #3 hole provides the lineup continuity we require, even as we monitor the \"Lineup Pending\" status for him and several others. \n\nWe must remain vigilant regarding the \"Lineup Pending\" flags attached to **Drake Baldwin**, **Nasim Nunez**, **Miguel Vargas**, **Sam Antonacci**, **Jackson Merrill**, **Kyle Tucker**, and **Luis Robert Jr.**, as any downward shifts in their batting order will erode the value added by their platoon advantages. Furthermore, while **Kyle Tucker** (58.86) and **Luis Robert Jr.** (61.82) are in the lineup, they are facing relatively stingy arms in Lake Bachar and Sean Newcomb. We have already accounted for the unavailability of **Andy Pages**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Jacob Wilson** due to injury; should any of our active starters receive a rest day, our depth is currently constrained, leaving us reliant on the high-upside potential of **Coby Mayo** (62.44) to sustain our production in the middle of the order.",
